			<div class="content" id="post-content-1879085">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">anything&nbsp;specific</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hail&nbsp;the&nbsp;nitpicks</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Floor B24 has become a habitat for several types of sentient autonomous sculptures, grouped into two categories, SCP-1619-1 and SCP-1619-2. Floor B24's environment contains various art supplies and furniture, which primarily consists of modern glass tables and office chairs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You establish that B24 is a dimensional anomaly, than mention -1 and -2, than go back to describing the layout of B24, then go back to the critters. Switching the second paragraph with the third would help. Also the details about furniture look out of place right next to -1.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Floor B24 consists of various hallways, rooms, and observatories, but lacks any doors.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That made me think that there's just drawings of doors on the walls similar to what happened to exits from the floor, and I was puzzled about how everyone goes from room to room until the field log. Maybe mention something about empty doorways.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>has the same appearance and texture of canvas paper.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Either &quot;has the appearance and texture of canvas paper&quot;, or &quot;has the same appearance and text as canvas paper&quot;. Former is better, imo.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>French documents and sketches have been recovered from within rooms containing one or more desks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is kinda weird. Maybe &quot;Sketches and documents written in French have been recovered from the desks present within SCP-1619&quot;. On than note, you use Floor B24 a lot, to the point that it becomes repetitive; maybe interchange it with SCP-1619 here and there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>are analogous female humanoid sculptures</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Analogous looks weird here and I'm not sure what you mean by that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Instances do not appear to notice or give</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Entities&quot; or &quot;sculptures&quot; would fit better here. I think &quot;instance(s)&quot; as a standalone noun looks weird pretty much everywhere, it's always &quot;instance(s) of SCP-1619-1&quot; or &quot;SCP-1619-1 instances&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Either the act of killing a SCP-1619-1 instance, or breaking a light bulb is sufficient in preventing an instance's bulb from dimming.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's not very clear how that works. I get that when a -2 kills a -1, the bulb of -2 is re-lit, but what's with the breaking of a bulb? Do you break the bulb that is the head of -2 (which yeah would prevent it from dimming, seeing how it's broken, but that's a weird thing to mention), or do you break a non-anomalous bulb near the -2 and then -2 isn't dimming anymore because you scared it by breaking the bulb, or does the -2 needs to break a light bulb? Hm, actually I think it's the later, seeing how some -2s hunt other -2s, but it isn't immediately clear from the context.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and restrain victims to the ground.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is kinda weirdly phrased</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the attacking SCP-1619-1 will release 30 ml of paint into the mouth of the victim.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The 30ml part seems unnecessarily specific here. Is it 30ml per second, or total, and how was it measured, seeing how the paint also self-replicates? Imo just &quot;will release paint into the mouth&quot; would be fine.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Attempts of removing this caricature</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Attempts to remove this caricature&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1619-1 is mainly considered prey by most SCP-1619-2 instances. SCP-1619-1's ineffective hunting methods, slow speeds, and lack of interest in SCP-1619-2</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;are mainly considered prey&quot;, &quot;slow speed&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1619-2 instances that only attack SCP-1619-1s instinctively are designated SCP-1619-2-B and have a small hole in the middle of their face-plate, which releases a thin beam of light.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This would work better as two sentences: &quot;[&#8230;] are designated SCP-1619-2-B. The constructs have a small hole in the middle [&#8230;]&quot;. Also saying that -B &quot;only attack SCP-1619-1s instinctively&quot; implies that there are other -2 specimens that only attack -1, but not based on instincts.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

